the Asians?\u00a0On what basis can we label Asians\u00a0an ethnic group? Although there is a significant Asian presence in the Caribbean, the category Asian\u00a0itself does not exist in the Caribbean. What does this say about the nature of categories that label and demarcate groups of people on the basis of alleged cultural and phenotypical characteristics? This course will examine the dynamics behind group identity, namely ethnicity, by comparing and contrasting the multicultural experience of Asian populations in the Caribbean and the United States. Ethnographic case studies will focus on the East Indian and Chinese experiences in the Caribbean and the Chinese, Korean, Japanese, Filipino, and Indian experiences in the United States.", "catalogBreadth": "(HB)", "catalogDistr": "(CA-AS, GLC-AS)", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "(EC-SAP)", "catalogWhenOffered": "Spring.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": null}, {"strm": 2783, "crseId": 351007, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "AAS", "catalogNbr": "4950", "titleShort": "Independent Study", "titleLong": "Independent Study", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "IND", "ssrComponentLong": "Independent Study", "section": "603", "classNbr": 7231, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "", "timeEnd": "", "startDt": "02/08/2021", "endDt": "05/14/2021", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "vpm1", "firstName": "Viranjini", "middleName": "P.", "lastName": "Munasinghe"}], "pattern": "", "facilityDescr": "Online Meeting", "bldgDescr": "Virtual", "facilityDescrshort": "Online", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes